{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>But you have not…</b> The meaning is that this good that I will do for My people is not an obligation, for even Israel in Babylon did not call upon Me:" "And the meaning of <b>for you have wearied</b> is: you did not even call upon Me, [so] that you would grow weary on My account:" "And the meaning of <b>Israel</b> is a vocative, like 'you are Israel.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {0 "The bracketed note [צ\"ל שאעשה] indicates the editor's correction: read 'that I will do' for the manuscripts' 'that he did.'", 1 "Parsing Ibn Ezra's compressed syntax is uncertain; the logic appears to be that they never even called Him, let alone wearied themselves for Him."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:50.249952054Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}